# Force LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks files out with CRLF while
# Prettier's endOfLine default is "lf" — so `npm run format:check`, part of the documented
# pre-push gate, fails on all ~111 files locally while passing in CI on Linux. Pinning LF
# here makes the gate mean the same thing on both.
#
# Nothing changes in the repository itself: Git already stores LF. This only governs what
# lands in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
